npost.com/lifestyle/2026/06/07/this-couple-grows-trees-shape-chairs-they-sell-90k/</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/tuesday-assorted-links-572.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tuesday-assorted-links-572">Tuesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.washingtonpost.com/lifestyle/2026/06/07/this-couple-grows-trees-shape-chairs-they-sell-90k/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.washingtonpost.com/lifestyle/2026/06/07/this-couple-grows-trees-shape-chairs-they-sell-90k/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 15:57:55 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[More comments on phones and fertility]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2052934494601048065/6TvQIpAs_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Neeraja Deshpande (@neerajadeshp) on X</p><p>I know this paper aligns with “it’s the phones,” aka the current theory of everything, but the idea that 1/3 to 1/2 of American TFR decline post-2007 was caused by smartphones is absurd. Some concerns: (1) It looks at AT&amp;T expansion from 2008-2011, which precedes the era of</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/neerajadeshp/status/2064017467840586147">https://x.com/neerajadeshp/status/2064017467840586147</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/tuesday-assorted-links-572.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tuesday-assorted-links-572">Tuesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/neerajadeshp/status/2064017467840586147</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/neerajadeshp/status/2064017467840586147</guid><pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 15:57:55 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gordon Wood, RIP]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/08/books/gordon-s-wood-dead.html">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/08/books/gordon-s-wood-dead.html</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/tuesday-assorted-links-572.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tuesday-assorted-links-572">Tuesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/08/books/gordon-s-wood-dead.html</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/08/books/gordon-s-wood-dead.html</guid><pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 15:57:55 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[It seems Piketty has become a degrowther]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HJ6gSPpWEAAAdrP.png:large"></p><p>Thomas Piketty (@PikettyWIL) on X</p><p>The key finding of the report is that energy transition alone will not suffice. We need to combine it with “sufficiency” to stay within 2 degrees. This includes labour hour reductions, growth caps in rich countries, less material consumption, and changes in food habits.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61">https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/monday-assorted-links-563.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=monday-assorted-links-563">Monday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/pikettywil/status/2062413196967784652?s=61</guid><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 16:43:05 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Luis Garicano 🇪🇺🇺🇦 (@lugaricano) on X]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1088718721785434112/TCQN0rTD_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Luis Garicano 🇪🇺🇺🇦 (@lugaricano) on X</p><p>This plan is incompatible with freedom- a global class of planners telling us how long to work, how much we can grow, what we can eat. It is also completely wrong. All advances for climate (including the huge drop in battery and solar and wind costs) have come (and will come)</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/lugaricano/status/2062948364283785527">https://x.com/lugaricano/status/2062948364283785527</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/monday-assorted-links-563.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=monday-assorted-links-563">Monday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/lugaricano/status/2062948364283785527</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/lugaricano/status/2062948364283785527</guid><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 16:43:05 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[a bit more]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1636256290866331649/set0qPh6_200x200.jpg"></p><p>tyro (@DoubleEph) on X</p><p>Important to remember that the reason anyone even bothers responding to that crap thread by Piketty is because when Capital In The 21st Century came out more than a decade ago, economists and media were falling over themselves to give it glowing reviews (because he incorporated</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/DoubleEph/status/2063925479678116183">https://x.com/DoubleEph/status/2063925479678116183</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/monday-assorted-links-563.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=monday-assorted-links-563">Monday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/DoubleEph/status/2063925479678116183</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/DoubleEph/status/2063925479678116183</guid><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 16:43:05 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Claims about soil]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://jf.x.com/images/media-preview/2062994923801243845"></p><p>Hereafter (@idyllicmusing) on X</p><p>Soil fertility alone explains 34% of the differences in national IQ. Countries on the best soils (Mollisols, Andisols) average 10–15 IQ points higher than those on the wort soils (Oxisols, Ultisols), even before accounting for education or income. This geographi